      "title": "Director of Donor Relations and Planned Giving",
      "description": "Director of Donor Relations and Planned Giving | Blackburn College All Jobs All Jobs Director of Donor Relations and Planned Giving Blackburn College Director of Donor Relations and Planned Giving Adjunct • Blackburn College At Blackburn College, every role makes a difference. Our faculty and staff are mentors, collaborators, and an essential part of a close-knit campus community dedicated to student success.\n\nWhether you're inspiring students in the classroom, supporting them behind the scenes, coaching the next generation, or helping our campus thrive, you'll have the opportunity to make a meaningful impact every day. Responsive recruiter Blackburn College is seeking an experienced fundraising and donor relations professional to serve as our Director of Donor Relations and Planned Giving during an exciting period of growth for the College. The Director will help build on this momentum by strengthening donor relationships, enhancing stewardship efforts, and expanding Blackburn’s planned giving program. Blackburn has experienced a multi-year enrollment surge, including a 19% increase in new freshman students over the prior year and a 39% increase in enrollment since fall 2024. The College also achieved record-breaking fundraising results last year, reflecting the strength and generosity of the Blackburn community. At the heart of this momentum is Blackburn’s commitment to expanding access, affordability, and opportunity. Thirty-six percent of Blackburn students are first-generation college students, 63% receive Pell Grants, and 40% represent racially and ethnically diverse backgrounds. About the Position Reporting to the Vice President for Institutional Advancement, the Director of Donor Relations and Planned Giving will develop and lead a comprehensive donor stewardship program designed to strengthen donor relationships, increase donor retention, and encourage future giving. The Director will oversee donor stewardship and recognition programs, gift acknowledgments, donor impact reporting, and other initiatives that create meaningful connections between donors and the impact of their support. The Director will also serve as Blackburn’s primary resource for planned giving, building relationships with planned giving prospects and members of the Heritage Society, Blackburn’s legacy giving society. Through donor engagement, educational outreach, and collaboration with colleagues across Institutional Advancement, the Director will help grow Blackburn’s planned giving program and strengthen the College’s long-term philanthropic future. Key Responsibilities Develop donor communications that demonstrate the impact of philanthropic support and Blackburn’s continued momentum. Oversee gift acknowledgment, donor recognition, stewardship, and impact-reporting programs. Build and maintain meaningful relationships with donors, planned giving prospects, and Heritage Society members. Develop marketing and communication strategies that educate alumni and friends about legacy giving opportunities and encourage future giving. Collaborate with Institutional Advancement colleagues to incorporate planned giving opportunities into donor conversations and cultivation strategies. Manage stewardship reporting for endowed and restricted funds and collaborate with campus partners to help ensure funds are used according to donor intent. Monitor donor retention, engagement, and stewardship efforts and identify opportunities for continued improvement. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required. At least three years of direct experience in a nonprofit fundraising environment preferred, particularly experience with donor stewardship or recognition programs. Excellent written, verbal, editing, and interpersonal communication skills. Strong organizational and project management skills with exceptional attention to detail. Ability to manage multiple priorities, meet deadlines, take initiative, exercise sound judgment, and work collaboratively with a wide range of constituents. Proficiency in Microsoft Office and the ability to quickly learn new software systems; experience with Blackbaud Raiser’s Edge and/or ADAVICO is preferred. Flexibility to occasionally work evenings and weekends for College and Institutional Advancement events. Willingness to travel occasionally as needed. Commitment to Blackburn College’s mission and an appreciation for the transformative impact of a liberal arts education and the College’s nationally recognized Work Program. Salary Range: $55,000–$65,000, commensurate with experience and qualifications. About Blackburn College Blackburn College is a private, residential liberal arts college located in Carlinville, Illinois. Blackburn is nationally recognized for its student-centered mission, strong sense of community, and distinctive Work Program, which provides students with meaningful leadership and employment experiences as they pursue their degrees. Blackburn College features a robust benefits package. For additional information, please visit https://blackburn.edu/about/administrative-offices/human-resources/ and click on the Employee Benefits Summary Tab. Blackburn College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and seeks to build an inclusive community that can engage the interests of a diverse population. We are committed to fostering, cultivating, and sustaining a culture that reflects the diversity of our country, and as such we particularly encourage applications from members of underrepresented groups such as women, people of color, LGBTQ+, veterans, and those with disabilities. Employment-based immigration sponsorship is not offered for this position. Phone calls or walk-ins not accepted. Applications will continue to be accepted until the position has been filled. Compensation: $55,000.00 - $65,000.00 per year We are an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive\n  consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex,\n  national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other\n  characteristic protected by law. Blackburn College is more than a place to work — it’s a community where your work makes an impact. Located in Carlinville, Illinois, Blackburn is a distinctive four-year liberal arts college known for combining a rigorous, affordable education with our nationally recognized student-managed Work Program . Our unique approach brings work, learning, and leadership together, giving students opportunities to develop skills and experience that extend far beyond the classroom. At Blackburn, faculty and staff play an important role in creating an environment where students are known, supported, challenged, and encouraged to grow. Whether you're teaching in the classroom, supporting campus operations, coaching student-athletes, or working behind the scenes, every position contributes to the Blackburn experience. What Makes Blackburn Different? Student-Centered — Our close-knit campus creates opportunities to build meaningful connections with students and colleagues. A One-of-a-Kind Work Program — Blackburn is home to a distinctive student-managed Work Program that gives students hands-on experience, responsibility, and leadership opportunities. A True Campus Community — Faculty, staff, and students work together to support the College and one another. Opportunity to Make an Impact — At a smaller institution, your ideas, expertise, and contributions are seen and valued. A Mission That Matters — We are committed to providing an accessible, high-quality education while preparing students for meaningful careers, community engagement, and lifelong learning. Come build your career at Blackburn College — and help our students build theirs. (if you already have a resume on Indeed) Or apply here. * required fields First Name * Last Name * Email * Phone * Text me updates about my application Yes No Message and data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Reply STOP to opt out.